{
  "version": "0.2",
  "readme": {
    "note": "Generic part/connector-driven simulation, now powered by the SHIPPED default script -- every part's script field is just \"return CommonScript_GenericPartActions(ctx);\", the one script every new Part ships with by default (see state.js's DEFAULT_BATCH_SCRIPT_CODE), left ENABLED here. That one shared function drives everything: behavior comes from ctx.part.type (INITIATOR/RESPONDER/passthrough) and each connector's relationship, never a hardcoded part id or label -- pass an optional second argument (initiatorTypes/responderTypes/relationshipActions) to override just the classification instead of writing a bespoke script. Only connectorType 'c' is used/read (the 's' Stream layer is a separate concern and is ignored). Every packet's subject is the sender's rawLabel. Flow 1: 'Business User' (BusinessActor, initiator) triggers 'Handle Product Inquiry' (BusinessProcess), which is served by 'Product Catalog Service' (ApplicationService), realized by 'Product Catalog System' (ApplicationComponent), which accesses the 'Product' data entity (DataDataEntity, responder) -- the reply then relays back up the same chain, one hop per tick, to Business User. Flow 2: 'Finance Department' (BusinessOrganizationUnit, initiator) polls its three BusinessCapability parts ('Budgeting', 'Reporting', 'Compliance' -- each a responder) every tick and logs each capability's status reply directly (no intermediate hops). Run/Step the simulation and watch the Message/Activity/Debug Log tabs (left sidebar) and each node's badges."
  },
